	affiliations = {School of Control and Computer Engineering, North China Electric Power University, Beijing, 102206, China; State Key Laboratory of Alternate Electrical Power System with Renewable Energy Sources, North China Electric Power University, Beijing, 102206, China; Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, National University of Singapore, Singapore, 117576, Singapore},
	abstract = {Fast and reliable load following is increasingly required as variable wind and photovoltaic generation expand. Combined-cycle gas turbines (CCGTs) are widely adopted to provide this flexibility. In a “2+1” CCGT, two gas turbines (GTs) are directly actuated, whereas the shared steam turbine (ST) contributes delayed power through heat-recovery and steam-cycle dynamics. A hierarchical framework combining improved model-free adaptive predictive control (IMFAPC), an extended state observer (ESO), and multi-agent proximal policy optimization (MAPPO), termed MAPPO-IMFAPC-ESO, is developed. A data-driven digital twin is formed from dynamic GT surrogates and a history-dependent ST model. Deterministic nominal commands are generated by ESO-enhanced IMFAPC (ESO-IMFAPC). Scaled and bounded residual corrections are allocated by MAPPO from local GT observations and the shared gross-generation error. Under a uniform contraction condition and bounded aggregate remainders, a conditional uniform ultimate boundedness estimate is derived for the exact-solve baseline. The fixed-policy implementation is characterized by conditional input-to-state practical stability under bounded deployment perturbations. Chronological leave-one-dataset-out validation confirms high one-step predictive accuracy of the ST model, with an RMSE of 1.920 MW and R<sup>2</sup>=0.9874, while held-out recursive command-replay tests reveal appreciable long-horizon error accumulation in the coupled GT–ST surrogate. Accordingly, the closed-loop results are interpreted as relative controller comparisons within a common learned digital-twin environment. Across five independently trained MAPPO-IMFAPC-ESO policies, the staircase gross-generation RMSE is 0.919 ± 0.014 MW, demonstrating repeatable sub-MW tracking, and a separate 24-hour evaluation shows no progressive growth of tracking error. Overall, the results demonstrate that the proposed hierarchical framework provides a unified data-driven approach for 