	abstract = {Photovoltaic noise barriers (PVNBs), as a new infrastructure for integrating transportation and energy, can realize the dual functions of noise reduction and photovoltaic power generation. Meanwhile, it also faces the strong nonlinear and multi-time scale characteristics caused by the coupling of dynamic changes in traffic flow and random fluctuations in meteorological conditions, which makes the precise modeling and real-time optimal control of the system operation state a significant challenge. In this study, a multi-objective model predictive control (MPC) strategy for PVNBs considering the dynamic coupling of traffic flow and weather conditions is proposed. Firstly, the coupling mechanism model of traffic flow-meteorology-photovoltaic-acoustic multi-physical fields is constructed, which reveals the synergistic influence mechanism of traffic flow, speed, irradiance, temperature, wind speed, and other factors on power generation and noise reduction effect. Then, through a convolutional neural network, it designs a CNN-LSTM-Attention hybrid prediction model to extract local spatio-temporal characteristics. Through long-term and short-term memory network, it captures temporal dependence. Besides, it focuses on key factors through an attention mechanism, which achieves accurate multi-step prediction of photovoltaic output and noise level. Furthermore, the entropy weight-AHP dynamic weight mechanism is introduced, which considers both objective data-driven and subjective expert experience. Besides, adjusting the weight ratio of power generation efficiency and noise control target in real time strengthens the robustness and scene adaptability of the control strategy. Compared to the traditional PID control and single-objective MPC, the proposed strategy increases the power generation efficiency by 8.3%–12.7%, the noise control accuracy by 15.2%–21.5%, and the fluctuation range of equipment operation by 23.4%–30.1%. Obviously, the grid adaptability meets th