	abstract = {Short-term photovoltaic power forecasting plays a vital role in the operation of photovoltaic power systems and grid management, as accurate predictions can provide more comprehensive information support for optimized grid oper- ation.This study proposes a deep learning algorithm named TCR-Reformer (Short-Term Photovoltaic Power Forecasting Using a Reformer-Based Model with Multi-Scale Dynamic Temporal Convolution and Enhanced Invertible Instance Normalization), aiming to address the challenges of data distribution shift and multi-scale temporal feature coupling in photovoltaic power forecasting.The framework integrates two core innovative modules:Adversarial Reversible Instance Normalization (AdvReVin) and Multi-Scale Dy-namic Temporal Convolutional Network (MS-DTCN). AdvReVin explicitly handles non-stationary data distributions across different weather patterns through adversarial training,while MS-DTCN captures local abrupt changes and long-term trends using varying dilation rates. Experiments based on real-world data collected in Guizhou Province from 2022 to 2024 demonstrate that the proposed method achieves a forecasting accuracy of 75.67% under the evaluation criteria of China Southern Power Grid.Compared with classic models such as Transformer, Informer, Autoformer, iTransformer, and Reformer, the proposed approach improves forecasting accuracy by 1%–3% and reduces the Mean Absolute Error (MAE) by approximately 15%. Experimental results further indicate that the model significantly enhances forecasting robustness under extreme weather conditions and seasonal transitions, providing reliable support for the stability of new-type power systems. Copyright © 2026. Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
