	affiliations = {Institute of Electrical and Control Engineering, Liaoning Technical University, Huludao, 125100, China; Institute of Intelligence Science and Engineering, Shenzhen Polytechnic University, Shenzhen, 518055, China},
	abstract = {Accurate photovoltaic (PV) power forecasting is crucial for the reliable operation of smart grids. However, the intermittency and nonlinearity of solar irradiance, especially under the abrupt weather conditions, poses significant challenges to PV power forecasting. To address the issues, a multistage PV power forecasting strategy integrating multi-granularity information and trend perception fusion mechanism under uncertain weather conditions is proposed in this paper, corresponding to coarse-grained and fine-grained forecasting stages. In the coarse-grained stage, a BiLSTM network with attention mechanism is employed to capture global temporal trends. For the fine-grained stage, adjacent features and similar features are explored to describe local fluctuation details. In detail, BiLSTM integrating empirical mode decomposition is designed for adjacent feature forecasting. Meanwhile, a novel dual-path Transformer model combining convolutional neural network encoding and K-means clustering is constructed for similar feature forecasting. Besides, a trend perception dynamic weight fusion strategy with Bayesian optimization is developed to adaptively integrate the forecasting results of different models. Finally, the proposed model achieves superior overall forecasting performance across real datasets, especially in terms of root mean square error reduction and fitting consistency. © 2026 IOP Publishing Ltd. All rights, including for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies, are reserved. This article is available under the terms of the IOP-Standard License.},
