	affiliations = {Shanghai Electric Power Company, Shanghai, China; Shanghai University of Electric Power, Shanghai, China},
	abstract = {As the popularity of renewable energy continues to increase, unpredictability and uncertainty are becoming major bottlenecks in the development of renewable energy. Forecasts are often used to predict renewable energy generation, but forecast errors can have significant negative impacts on power system performance. However, current research often overlooks the impact of spatial correlation or disrupts the original graph structure in regard to the fusion of spatial and temporal correlations. Therefore, this study describes a deep learning technology based on spatiotemporal analysis for accurate solar power prediction. This paper proposes a generative adversarial adaptive graph convolutional network (GAAGCN) method, which utilizes graph neural networks to capture spatial correlations using dynamic and static adaptive adjacency matrices and employs temporal convolutional networks to extract temporal correlations. Generative adversarial networks further enhance the prediction accuracy. Our model effectively captures the spatiotemporal correlation of real solar power generation datasets, achieving a 5.1% improvement over the best past models on our dataset. © 2026 Chinese Academy of Sciences.},
