	abstract = {With growing concerns about the environment and the rising risks and costs associated with fossil fuels, today's power systems are rapidly transitioning toward renewable energy sources. While subsidies and incentives often drove early adoption, renewable energy producers now face the challenge of competing in open electricity markets while ensuring profitability. This paper presents an AI-enhanced bidding strategy for a virtual power plant (VPP) that integrates wind and solar generation with demand response (DR) capabilities. At the core of the proposed hybrid approach is a Non-Dominated Sorting Genetic Algorithm II (NSGA-II) and Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) neural network that forecasts wind power output, PV generation, market prices, and demand profiles for the day-ahead horizon. These forecasts feed into a multi-objective optimization framework that strategically allocates DR resources and determines optimal market bids. Technically, this framework enhances grid reliability by minimizing Expected Energy Not Supplied (EENS), reducing active power losses, and lowering outage-related consumer costs. Commercially, the strategy enhances profitability by anticipating market conditions and minimizing imbalance settlement costs through optimal DR deployment. The method is validated on the IEEE 24-bus test system, demonstrating strong performance in both market outcomes and system reliability.  © 2026 The Authors.},
