	affiliations = {Mechanical & Mechatronics Engineering Department, College of Engineering, Dhofar University, Salalah, Oman; Electrical Engineering Department, University of Technology and Applied Science, Nizwa, Oman; Marine Engineering Department, Military Technological College, Muscat, Oman; Architectural Engineering Department, College of Engineering, Dhofar University, Salalah, Oman},
	abstract = {Accurate forecasting is essential in integrating photovoltaic (PV) output power into the grid. Solar energy has become critical for many countries recently, but the fact that PV power generation is intermittent impacts the operation of existing grids quite significantly. In order to reduce this uncertainty and safeguard the system, a precise technique for forecasting solar power is needed. This study examined indirect, direct, and hybrid strategies, with particular emphasis on those based on machine and deep learning. Due to interruptions caused by PV power generation, which downgrades the stability of the grid, accurate prediction models are important for energy systems. This article offers a sound evaluation and comprehensive summary of the various methods that are currently used to forecast the output of solar power systems. The survey results suggest that solar power forecasting requires feature extraction and data processing capabilities, a strong deep learning structure to train with, and an ability to evaluate uncertainty to be fully functional and complete. © 2026 Institute of Physics Publishing. All rights reserved.},
