	abstract = {This systematic review explores the transformative potential of artificial intelligence (AI) in revolutionizing energy management for smart homes, with a particular lens on enhancing the lives of Nigerian residential electricity users. A diverse array of AI models—ranging from Reinforcement Learning and Deep Learning to Gradient Boosting and optimization algorithms— demonstrates remarkable capabilities in predicting energy needs, scheduling appliances, and optimizing resource use. These models leverage technologies like IoT sensors, photovoltaic systems, and cloud platforms to deliver precise control and adaptability, offering a beacon of hope for Nigeria’s erratic power landscape. The benefits are compelling: substantial cost reductions of up to 42.9%, energy savings peaking at 33%, and enhanced sustainability through a 60% CO₂ reduction, all while maintaining household comfort. For Nigerian households grappling with high tariffs and frequent outages, these advancements promise lower bills, reliable power via solar integration, and a greener future. However, the journey to widespread adoption faces hurdles—complex model training and infrastructure gaps demand attention. This paper concludes that AI holds the key to empowering Nigeria’s energy future, bridging individual needs with grid stability, provided policy issues are sorted and the right investments are made in this area to tackle the challenge. © 2025 NIPES Pub.},
