	abstract = {The necessity for sustainable development and the adoption of renewable energy sources, notably photovoltaic (PV) solar power, is underscored by the expanding global need for energy. The integration of solar electricity into current energy networks creates challenges despite its tremendous potential to reduce environmental issues. This is especially true given its intermittent nature, which is influenced by meteorological circumstances. Precise short-term forecasting is important to assure grid stability and proper energy management in light of this volatility. Our work provides a forecasting method utilizing a hybrid model architecture that integrates bidirectional layers of Gated Recurrent Units (GRU), Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM), and Efficient Channel Attention (ECA) with Temporal Convolutional Networks (TCNs). Forecast accuracy is significantly increased by this model, which successfully takes into account both long-term dependencies. With a remarkable configuration of TCN ECANet STACKED BiLSTMBiGRU, our model performs remarkably well when evaluated on the DKASC dataset from Uluru, Australia. It achieves an average RMSE of 0.028975, MAE of 0.0119275, and R² Score of 0.98832. This study extends the capabilities for precise solar power forecasting and helps to strategically incorporate renewable energy sources into the grid, along with more general sustainability goals. © 2025},
