	affiliations = {School of Artificial Intelligence, China University of Geosciences, Beijing, 100083, China; Transmission and Transformation Engineering Technology Branch, State Grid Electric Power Engineering Research Institute, Beijing, 100069, China; School of Engineering and Technology, China University of Geosciences, Beijing, 100083, China},
	abstract = {Photovoltaic power generation is invariably confronted with the global maximal power point (GMPP) tracking issue in partial shading conditions. Machine learning has greatly expedited photovoltaic power prediction, yet few works pay attention to the cost-effective construction of high-quality GMPP dataset in this field. This paper proposes a method for constructing hybrid dataset assisted by cross-validation for predicting GMPP in partial shading conditions with both cost-effectiveness and sufficient accuracy. Specifically, GMPP data are mixed with abundant maximal power point data under uniform irradiation in proportion optimized by the cross-validation. Through iteratively training and optimizing the artificial neural network via the hybrid dataset, the prediction error steadily decreases as the mixing ratio of the GMPP data increases, proving that limited dataset inconsistency between the training and testing set renders satisfactory accuracy. With 10 % GMPP data mixed, the average prediction accuracy reaches 97.2 % in simulation and 96.4 % in experiment. This indicates that the acquisition cost of the GMPP data can be reduced by 90 %, while the prediction accuracy loss is only 2.8 % in simulation and 3.6 % in experiment, proving the balanced cost-effectiveness and accuracy of the proposed hybrid dataset construction method in photovoltaic power forecast application. © 2025 The Authors},
