	abstract = {As a clean energy source, accurate prediction of photovoltaic power generation is crucial to grid stability and energy management. This study proposes a spatiotemporal prediction model based on convolutional neural network (CNN) and long short-term memory network (LSTM). CNN extracts spatial features, and LSTM models time series dependencies. Experimental results show that the CNN-LSTM model performs well under different meteorological and geographical conditions, and its prediction accuracy is significantly higher than that of traditional methods and single deep learning models. The model has a MSE of 40.12, a MAE of 3.85, and an R² of 0.94 in clear summer weather, showing strong adaptability and robustness. Under cloudy conditions in winter, despite large fluctuations in meteorological data, the model can still maintain a stable prediction effect. This model provides an efficient and accurate solution for photovoltaic power generation prediction, which can effectively support energy scheduling and management and promote the widespread application of photovoltaic energy.  © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).},
