	affiliations = {Amrita School of Engineering, Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Coimbatore, 641112, India; Florida Atlantic University, Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science, Boca Raton, 33431, FL, United States},
	abstract = {Digital twins (DTs) are emerging as transformative tools for the monitoring, control, and optimization of photovoltaic (PV) systems. While prior studies have addressed aspects such as MPPT (Maximum Power Point Tracking), forecasting, and inverter control in isolation, a cohesive, system-level integration remains underexplored. This paper proposes a unified functional architecture for DTs in PV applications, encompassing real-time monitoring, signal processing, control synchronization, and AI-enabled forecasting. We systematically categorize the enabling technologies—including IoT platforms, edge–cloud orchestration, and cyber–physical system (CPS) integration—and analyze their roles across the DT lifecycle. Furthermore, case-driven evaluations illustrate practical implementation challenges, performance metrics, and deployment strategies. The proposed framework offers a scalable and interoperable blueprint to guide the development of intelligent DT infrastructures for next-generation solar energy systems. © 2013 IEEE.},
