	abstract = {This paper proposes a distributed photovoltaic power prediction model based on Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition (EEMD) and Fuzzy Cognitive Maps (FCMs). By utilizing EEMD to decompose and reconstruct photovoltaic power time series data, the impact of non-stationary time series is mitigated. Then, the reconstructed data is used as the result nodes of FCMs, and the weight matrix is solved using the Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) algorithm to construct the prediction model. Experimental results show that the model has high accuracy in photovoltaic power prediction in different seasons, and it performs better than traditional FCMs, BP neural networks, and LSTM models in terms of prediction accuracy and training time, providing an effective new method for the accurate prediction of distributed photovoltaic power. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s)},
