	abstract = {Te fght against global warming is becoming increasingly important because of the race to fnd new sources of energy. Tis work presents a method for estimating solar energy (SE) potential by applying LSTM neural networks to predict the parameters infuencing photovoltaic production, namely, solar irradiation and temperature over 24 h. Te database comes from MERRA-2 and includes the meteorological parameters’ temperature, relative humidity, atmospheric pressure, wind speed, wind direction, solar irradiation and rainfall for 20 locations in northern Cameroon with hourly time steps over 23 years, from 2000 to 2022. Te method consists of designing an LSTM neural model to obtain the lowest deviation between the real and predicted data. Te performance criteria used to validate the model that predicts the two parameters are an accuracy of 92.45% and an RMSE of 20.9. Te model was tested in two localities, Makary and Banyo, with the most important values out of the 20 localities. Te database was used to estimate that the average SE potential is 2.193 MWh/m<sup>2</sup>/year in Makary, and the lowest potential is 1.949 MWh/m<sup>2</sup>/year in Banyo. Tis information can be used to select sites for solar power plant installations, solar photovoltaic energy management, solar electric vehicle (EV) feet management and to select sites for the construction of EV recharging stations. Copyright © 2024 Saito Douswekreo et al.},
