	abstract = {Artificial intelligence is considered as a true driver of Industry 4.0 revolution. Combined with the power of connected objects and Big data, it is already revolutionizing the industrial sector thus allowing the realization of short, medium and long-term predictions. In fact, to exploit the significant quantities of data from the entire industrial ecosystem, it is crucial to rely fundamentally on these technologies especially the use of Artificial intelligence-based algorithms. Therefore, the main goal of this paper is to use Machine learning algorithms as part of Artificial intelligence, to forecast the hourly power provided by photovoltaic panels. In particular, a comparison study of Ensemble methods including Bootstrap aggregating (Bagging), Random Forests, and Boosting is performed to decide which models have the best forecasting outcomes. The investigated models are then assessed using the most commonly evaluation criteria: R-squared, Root Mean Square Error, and Mean Absolute Error. Furthermore, model reliability is determined by examining residual plots of the respective predictive models. © 2021 Elsevier B.V.. All rights reserved.},
